# CI and Testing

## Local commands (mirror GitHub Actions)

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `pnpm run ci` | Fast gate: lint → typecheck → test:ci → build |
| `pnpm quality` | Full gate (same as CI `quality` job): + secret scan, security tests, audit |
| `pnpm lint` | ESLint, zero warnings |
| `pnpm typecheck` | Turbo typecheck across workspace |
| `pnpm test` | Unit + integration smoke tests |
| `pnpm test:ci` | CI test subset (no security tests) |
| `pnpm test:security` | Authz, leak scanner, Studio route guards |
| `pnpm security:audit` | Production dependency audit (high+) |
| `pnpm docs:check` | Required docs exist, basic Markdown sanity |

## Before every PR

```bash
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm quality
```

Do not push or mark a PR ready until `pnpm quality` exits 0.

## Test expectations

- Bug fixes should include a regression test when practical.
- New features need tests or documented manual QA steps in the PR.
- Security-sensitive changes must pass `pnpm test:security`.
- Touching `packages/database`? Run `pnpm --filter @uwe/database db:generate` before typecheck.

## Rules

- CI must not be greened with fake/no-op scripts.
- Fix root causes; do not disable checks without documented justification.
- Commit `pnpm-lock.yaml` after dependency changes.
- Prisma schema changes need migrations in `packages/database/prisma/migrations/`.

